  "query_preview": "..A trough remained centered off the California coast\nwith high pressure centered over Arkansas/Louisiana Saturday \nafternoon. The southerly flow between these two pressure systems \ncontinued to pull monsoon moisture northward but with the slight\nwestward shift of the high center over the past 24 hours the bulk\nof the deeper moisture is being directed up the Lower Colorado \nValley into southern Nevada. The nudging of the high center \ntoward Arizona has also brought some subsidence aloft with a \ncapping/stabilizing layer in the mid-levels.\n\nFor tonight...A few showers and thunderstorms could linger into\nthe early evening hours but after that we are anticipating a\ncomplete shutdown as subsidence and further stabilization occurs.\n\nFrom Sunday into Tuesday...The high pressure center gradually \nbuilds from over the southern United States to over Arizona. \nMonsoon moisture will remain at the lower limits for activity for \nmost of the area as well as a capping layer aloft adding further \nstabilization. As a result, most of northern Arizona will see only\nisolated afternoon and early evening showers and thunderstorms \nthrough the period. The exception, moisture values will remain \njust high enough over the high terrain of far eastern Arizona for \nscattered afternoon showers and thunderstorms, primarily the White\nMountains region. Otherwise, look for warmer temperatures and\nlight winds under the influence of the building high.\n\nLooking further out...It appears active monsoon weather will \nbe on the increase as the high pressure center finds it's way to \nthe Four Corners region, opening the door to increasing monsoon \nmoisture.",
